MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The step drill bits felt like a strong next choice because they would let me enlarge sheet-metal holes for projects using my rivets and rivet nuts, adding a capability beyond my existing drill bits.",
    "The foam mounting tape and rubber wiring grommets fit my repair work because they solve distinct problems: mounting parts with a thicker adhesive and protecting wires through drilled panels. Duct tape also fits my ongoing general repairs."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The pneumatic valve and hose shutoff valve require a specific setup and matching dimensions. My purchases of repair tools and fasteners do not mean I currently need either kind of valve.",
    "The cotter pins and M6 screws fit my interests, but my existing assortments may already cover them. Copper sealing washers and magnets are plausible workshop supplies, yet I have no immediate project requiring them."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in workshop repairs seems to have been stretched into an assumed need for specialized tubing and hose fittings.",
    "My repeated purchases of hardware assortments seem to have been treated as a reason to choose more similar supplies, even when I may already have enough."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "What matters most is whether an item adds a useful capability to tools I already own, as the step bits would for drilling and riveting work.",
    "Recent purchases affect what I need now: another cotter pin assortment is less useful after buying one, while rubber wiring grommets serve a different purpose from the eyelets used with my press."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understood my hands-on repair interests but sometimes confused related workshop supplies with a current need or a useful addition to what I own."
}
